The supplied backend report documents persistent person, portrait, Wish
Circle, wish, match, maker and Wish Book data. It also documents Wish
Maker applications and human approval, stricter verification for
in-person wishes, private contact details until acceptance,
feedback/concern handling, private invite links, expiry and deletion.
The engine contract specifies source labels, traceable wish metadata,
fallback behaviour and timeouts. Raw provider-derived Qloo response data
must not be published in public examples or fixtures.
Product journey
1. Start a story: Create a person using minimal details.
2. Taste Portrait: Add favourites and build a portrait with
   provenance.
3. Wish Circle: Collect memories from family through a private
   consent-based link.
4. Wishes: Generate personal ideas with source items and
   uncertainty labels.
5. Wish Makers: See matching suggestions, send requests and track
   accepted, declined, withdrawn or completed status.
6. Wish Book: Compile a keepsake, print it and optionally share it.
7. Privacy: Manage retention and deletion.
Other documented experiences include Reaction Mode, Compare, an agent
log/replay and a comfort-oriented Bedside Kit. The organisation pathway
has a public application and private coordination portal.
